 class="rank">5</div><div class="row-body"><div class="row1"><span class="name">KeystoneOS</span><span class="pill active">active</span></div><div class="purpose">Cross-harness memory, automation, and backup operating system</div><div class="next-action">Phase 3: port the backup path contract to macOS when the MacBook arrives (procedure in ~/.claude/MIGRATION-MACOS.md)</div><div class="stage-pipeline"><span class="segs"><span class="seg filled" title="idea"></span><span class="seg filled" title="grilled"></span><span class="seg filled" title="spec"></span><span class="seg filled" title="planned"></span><span class="seg filled" title="building"></span><span class="seg" title="shipped"></span></span><span class="stage-label">building 5/6</span></div><div class="plan-progress"><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:0%"></div></div><div class="bar-label">Plan: 0/62 tasks</div></div><div class="doc-chips"><span title="2026-08-02-durability-contract-and-ownership.md">spec</span> · <span title="2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md">plan</span></div><div class="stale-flag">⚠ 30d untouched</div><div class="update">2026-08-15 — Curation 2026-08-15: Essentially my operating system. A lot of things get routed through it. It is a router at this point. What it started out being, I&#x27;m not sure it is that anymore — it was going to be a place where a lot of projects were done, but I&#x27;ve started to use the DEV folder and just have individual projects be individual folders.</div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="rank">6</div><div class="row-body"><div class="row1"><span class="name">CFB_Analytics_Lab</span><span class="pill active">active</span></div><div class="purpose">A learning workspace for fluency in applying data-science techniques to football data — the methods in Eager &amp; Erickson&#x27;s Football Analytics with Python and R, transposed from the book&#x27;s NFL/nflfastR data onto college football data from the CollegeFootballData API. Fluency means choosing a method for a football question, fitting it, and explaining both what it says and where it breaks; each lesson ends in a drill completed unaided, and the drill is the evidence. Curriculum: over-expected metrics (CPOE/RYOE), GLMs, stability analysis, clustering + PCA, tree ensembles, and Bayesian hierarchical models (lesson 0007, a deliberate extension past the book). Explicitly out of scope: beating the betting market, Baylor coaching deliverables, and any change to CFB_Victory_Model.</div><div class="next-action">Review and merge PR #1, open since 2026-08-13 — the `foundation` branch, 21 commits ahead of `main`, with the three fix-before-merge rulings already applied in 02a190b — then complete Drill 0001 and report the result; lesson 0002 is gated on that drill</div><div class="stage-pipeline"><span class="segs"><span class="seg filled" title="idea"></span><span class="seg filled" title="grilled"></span><span class="seg filled" title="spec"></span><span class="seg filled" title="planned"></span><span class="seg filled" title="building"></span><span class="seg" title="shipped"></span></span><span class="stage-label">building 5/6</span></div><div class="plan-progress"><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:0%"></div></div><div class="bar-label">Plan: 0/58 tasks</div></div><div class="doc-chips"><span title="2026-08-13-cfb-analytics-lab-design.md">spec</span> · <span title="2026-08-13-cfb-analytics-lab-foundation.md">plan</span></div><div class="stale-flag">⚠ 30d untouched</div><div class="update">2026-08-15 — Curation 2026-08-15: A professional development project on the side to enhance my data science and analytical skills.</div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="rank">7</div><div class="row-body"><div class="row1"><span class="name">Project_Triage</span><span class="pill active">active</span></div><div class="purpose">This portfolio registry and front-burner dashboard</div><div class="next-action">Add a set-dev-folder verb to portfolio.py so new projects cannot register without a folder link</div><div class="stage-pipeline"><span class="segs"><span class="seg filled" title="idea"></span><span class="seg filled" title="grilled"></span><span class="seg filled" title="spec"></span><span class="seg filled" title="planned"></span><span class="seg filled" title="building"></span><span class="seg filled" title="shipped"></span></span><span class="stage-label">shipped 6/6</span></div><div class="plan-progress"><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:0%"></div></div><div class="bar-label">Plan: 0/49 tasks</div></div><div class="doc-chips"><span title="2026-09-14-prioritization-system-design.md">spec</span> · <span title="2026-08-15-portfolio-merge-and-board.md">plan</span></div><div class="stale-flag">⚠ 42d untouched</div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="rank">9</div><div class="row-body"><div class="row1"><span class="name">PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA</span><span class="pill active">active</span></div><div class="purpose">Why Baylor&#x27;s offense declined from 2024 to 2025, measured two ways on the same 1,935 charted plays. Joins the coaches&#x27; play-call chart to PFF&#x27;s play data and to CFBD&#x27;s expected-points model, then asks whether the two lenses agree. Success rate fell 57.4% to 49.5%; EPA (CFBD PPA) agrees on every headline cut. Early-down running is the sharpest cut under either lens and went below zero EPA in 2025 -- it cost expected points. Phase 4 decomposed the decline into mix versus efficacy and found it is efficacy: Baylor lined up the same, defenses lined up the same, and the same concepts produced less. Three data gates refuse to build tables on unvalidated joins, and every figure in the report is computed from a table rather than typed. Out of scope: opponent adjustment, player attribution, and any expected-points model of our own.</div><div class="next-action">Phase 3 (2026 weekly ingest) is blocked on three things, all tracked by a test: export 2026_All_Games.csv from PFF into the repo root; pull 2026 CFBD plays in CFB_Analytics_Lab; and ingest 2026 into pff.db in PFF_Data_Project (the week1_auburn JSON was never ingested). See docs/PHASE3-READINESS.md. Also decide whether a mid-season 2026 belongs in the same tables as two complete seasons.</div><div class="stage-pipeline"><span class="segs"><span class="seg filled" title="idea"></span><span class="seg filled" title="grilled"></span><span class="seg filled" title="spec"></span><span class="seg filled" title="planned"></span><span class="seg filled" title="building"></span><span class="seg" title="shipped"></span></span><span class="stage-label">building 5/6</span></div><div class="plan-progress"><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:0%"></div></div><div class="bar-label">Plan: 0/52 tasks</div></div><div class="doc-chips"><span title="2026-09-10-playcalls-phase5-opponent-adjustment-design.md">spec</span> · <span title="2026-09-10-playcalls-phase5-opponent-adjustment.md">plan</span></div><div class="update">2026-09-10 — Phase 2 and Phase 4 built, reviewed, merged and pushed. Phase 2 added EPA from CFBD PPA -- verified as a real expected-points model by drive reconciliation, not assumed -- plus score state, which Phase 1 had recorded as impossible. Gate 3 scores the join rather than the source at 96.7%, per season and overall. Phase 4 decomposed the decline: mix -0.5 points against efficacy -8.8, so alignment does not explain it. An adversarial Codex review found nine real defects past green tests, the worst being score state measured after the play rather than before it. All fixed. Also corrected two Phase 1 table defects and a stale 99.3% match rate that no artefact supported. 249 tests pass.</div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="rank">8</div><div class="row-body"><div class="row1"><span class="name">S2_Evaluation</span><span class="pill paused">paused</span></div><div class="purpose">Mine existing S2 Cognition testing data for actionable, coach-facing insights that go beyond normative percentiles — intra-athlete profile shape, change over time, position-relevant weighting, and decision-linked thresholds rather than normative ranking.</div><div class="next-action">Decide whether to run the same calibrated method on WR (n=13) and ILB (n=10), or stop here — and retest the one lineman whose S2 report failed vendor validity checks</div><div class="stage-pipeline"><span class="segs"><span class="seg filled" title="idea"></span><span class="seg filled" title="grilled"></span><span class="seg filled" title="spec"></span><span class="seg filled" title="planned"></span><span class="seg filled" title="building"></span><span class="seg filled" title="shipped"></span></span><span class="stage-label">shipped 6/6</span></div><div class="drift-flag">⚠ stage is shipped but no spec doc found</div><div class="update">2026-08-15 — Curation 2026-08-15: Looks at some testing data.</div></div></div><div class="lane-foot">9 projects</div></section></div>
